# 1️⃣ What is Dynamic Programming?

Dynamic Programming means:

```text
Store already computed answers
and reuse them.
```

Instead of solving the same problem repeatedly.

---

### Example

Fibonacci:

```text
F(5)

=
F(4) + F(3)

F(4)
=
F(3) + F(2)
```

Notice:

```text
F(3)
```

is computed multiple times.

DP avoids this repetition.

---

# 2️⃣ Overlapping Subproblems

A problem has overlapping subproblems if:

```text
Same subproblem
appears multiple times.
```

Example:

```text
Fib(5)

Fib(3)
appears repeatedly.
```

---

# 3️⃣ Optimal Substructure

A problem has optimal substructure if:

```text
Optimal solution
can be built from
optimal solutions of
smaller subproblems.
```

Example:

```text
Shortest Path

Knapsack

LCS
```

---

# 4️⃣ Two Ways to Solve DP

## Memoization

```text
Top Down
```

