# 5️⃣ Fibonacci Using Recursion

```cpp
int fib(int n)
{
    if(n <= 1)
        return n;

    return
    fib(n-1)
    +
    fib(n-2);
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(2^N)

Space: O(N)
```

Very slow.

---

# 6️⃣ Fibonacci Using Memoization

## Idea

Store answer once.

Reuse later.

---

### Code

```cpp
int solve(
    int n,
    vector<int>& dp)
{
    if(n <= 1)
        return n;

    if(dp[n] != -1)
        return dp[n];

    return dp[n] =
        solve(n-1, dp)
        +
        solve(n-2, dp);
}
```

---

### Driver

```cpp
vector<int> dp(
    n + 1,
    -1
);

cout <<
solve(n, dp);
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 7️⃣ Fibonacci Using Tabulation

## Idea

Build answer from smaller states.

---

### Code

```cpp
vector<int> dp(
    n + 1,
    0
);

dp[0] = 0;
dp[1] = 1;

for(int i=2;i<=n;i++)
{
    dp[i] =
    dp[i-1]
    +
    dp[i-2];
}

cout << dp[n];
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 8️⃣ Space Optimized Fibonacci

Observe:

```text
Only previous
two values needed.
```

---

### Code

```cpp
int prev2 = 0;
int prev1 = 1;

for(int i=2;i<=n;i++)
{
    int current =
        prev1 + prev2;

    prev2 = prev1;

    prev1 = current;
}

cout << prev1;
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(1)
```

